<article class="env-lemma" id="01Y4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01Y4">Lemma <span data-tag="01Y4">30.9.6</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$, $\mathcal{G}$ be coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Let $x \in X$. Suppose $\psi : \mathcal{G}_ x \to \mathcal{F}_ x$ is a map of $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-modules. Then there exists an open neighbourhood $U \subset X$ of $x$ and a map $\varphi : \mathcal{G}|_ U \to \mathcal{F}|_ U$ such that $\varphi _ x = \psi $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In view of Lemma <a href="/tag/01XZ" data-tag="01XZ">30.9.1</a> this is a reformulation of Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01CP" data-tag="01CP">17.22.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>